  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public service infrastructure development project in YemenPublic service infrastructure development project in Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">More than nine years of conflict in Yemen has destabilized communities, led to mass displacement and left millions of households grappling to meet their most basic needs. Local authorities and public service providers continued to lack resources and capacity to provide basic services, notably in areas hosting large, displaced populations. With the objective of increasing the resilience of communities to destabilizing forces stemming from the ongoing conflict, and competition for scarce resources and services, this project will improve local public service infrastructure and support social cohesion among diverse community members. Through ongoing interventions and existent community networks, IOM has identified water sanitation and hygiene (WASH), health and education infrastructure rehabilitation activities and will conduct further consultations and assessments at the start of the project to select community infrastructure projects that improve service provision and alleviate tensions in communities due to lack thereof. IOM is also conducting community building activities to further support communities in building channels for conflict resolution and trust building, so that communities are equipped to address future conflicts and stay resilient to polarizing influences.</narrative>
  </description>
